  lex_comments_err_escaped_end_space.pcpp - Lexical: a spliced closer with a blank

  Break step of lex_comments: a splice with a blank after its backslash
  between the star and the slash that close a block comment still
  closes it, and warns twice, as clang does: LX0202 (the escaped
  closer) at the backslash and LX0201 (the blank) right after it. The
  module builds. The marked line is inside the comment, so the comment
  itself carries the markers.
  Its bytes are part of the test (see above): edit it with an editor
  that keeps them as they are.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_comments_err_escaped_end_space;

/*
  @@test
    kind build
  @@end
*/

begin
  /* // WARN LX0202@68 // WARN LX0201@69 // the closer is spliced *\ 
/
end.
